_refine.details                                  
;INITIAL REFINEMENT CARRIED OUT WITH TNT AND XPLOR RESIDUES B 402 - B 409 INCLUSIVE HAVE BEEN GIVEN ZERO OCCUPANCY AS THERE WAS NO INTERPRETABLE ELECTRON DENSITY IN THIS REGION. THE POSITIONS OF SIDE CHAIN ATOMS WITH TEMPERATURE FACTORS GREATER THAN 75 IS UNCERTAIN. THE MAIN CHAIN CONFORMATION IS ALSO UNCERTAIN FOR REGIONS WITH TEMPERATURE FACTORS ABOVE 60. SOLVENT MOLECULES HAVE BEEN USED TO MODEL SOME FEATURES IN THE ELECTRON DENSITY THAT ARE PROBABLY DUE TO THE "MISSING" REGIONS OF THE GAMMA SUBUNIT (CHAIN G) THE PEPTIDE BOND BETWEEN ASP 269 AND ASP 270 IN CHAINS A, B, C AND THE PEPTIDE BOND BETWEEN ASP 256 AND ASN 257 IN CHAINS D, E, AND F HAVE BEEN MODELED IN A CIS CONFORMATION. RESIDUAL FEATURES IN THE ELECTRON DENSITY MAP SUGGEST THAT THERE IS SOME CONFORMATIONAL DISORDER IN ASP 270 IN CHAINS A, B, AND C. CRYSTALS WERE GROWN IN THE PRESENCE OF AZIDE, A KNOWN INHIBITOR, BUT THIS HAS NOT BEEN LOCATED IN THE STRUCTURE.
;
