_struct_biol.id        1 
_struct_biol.details   
;THE F1-ATPASE MOLECULE HAS THREE COPIES OF                   
  THENON-CATALYTIC ALPHA SUBUNIT AND THREE COPIES                     
 OF THECATALYTIC BETA SUBUNIT.IN THE PRIMARY                          
 REFERENCE, THE BETA SUBUNITS WERE LABELEDACCORDING                   
 TO THE BOUND NUCLEOTIDE, AS,BETA(DP) (BINDS ADP                      
 ),BETA(E) (NO BOUND NUCLEOTIDE) ANDBETA(TP) (                        
 AMPPNP BOUND).THE ALPHA SUBUNITS (WHICH ALL BIND                     
 AMPPNP) CONTRIBUTE TOTHE CATALYTIC SITES OF THE                      
 BETA SUBUNITS, AND HAVE BEENLABELED ACCORDINGLY.                     
 THUS,ALPHA(DP) CONTRIBUTES TO THE CATALYTIC SITE                     
 ON BETA(DP),ALPHA(TP) TO THE SITE ON BETA (                          
 TP) ANDALPHA(E)  TO THE SITE ON BETA(E).THE                          
 CORRESPONDENCE BETWEEN THE SUBUNIT NAMES AND THE                     
 CHAINIDENTIFIERS IS GIVEN BELOW:.CHAIN A: ALPHA(E                    
 )CHAIN B: ALPHA(TP)CHAIN C: ALPHA(DP)CHAIN D                         
 : BETA(DP)CHAIN E: BETA(E)CHAIN F: BETA(TP)                          
 CHAIN G: GAMMA SUBUNIT
;
# 
